%% Diagram: EventBridge Pipes - Source -> Filter -> Enrichment -> Target
%% Source lecture: AWS EventBridge Crash Course - Lecture: "EventBridge Pipes"
%% Description:  Shows the four stages of an EventBridge Pipe with the source,
%%               optional filter, optional enrichment, and target. In this
%%               example an SQS queue is the source, a JSON event pattern acts
%%               as the filter, a Lambda function enriches the payload, and
%%               the result is written to an S3 bucket.
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <prem.vishnoi@example.com>
```mermaid
graph LR
    SRC[Stage 1: Source<br/>SQS Queue<br/>order-events]
    F[Stage 2: Filter<br/>event pattern<br/>optional]
    ENR[Stage 3: Enrichment<br/>Lambda<br/>addCustomerProfile<br/>optional]
    TGT[Stage 4: Target<br/>S3 Bucket<br/>enriched-orders/]
    OUT[(Enriched Event<br/>delivered to target)]

    SRC --> F
    F -->|match| ENR
    F -->|drop| DROP[X Filtered Out]
    ENR --> TGT
    TGT --> OUT
```
